RE-TAKEN after JOURNAL.md entry 14. Two handicaps were found in this slice's
own incumbent arms and both are fixed here:
  * the encode baseline gp-writeto paid a top-level CalculateSize to size its
    span. gp-bufferwriter is the same official API family with no size pass at
    all, over a reused BufWriter that RESETS rather than clearing;
  * the decode baseline gp-parse ended with m.CalculateSize(), a full traversal
    of the decoded tree, while managed-parse returned a free offset. BOTH arms
    now park the graph in a static sink and return an O(1) value.
Every timing figure this slice published before 87a2e39b0c2cc28adbb05ab70b198f7b132828f3 is superseded.

build: /p:AkCount=true, the COUNTING build. The per-site store is behind
AK_COUNT and is not in the build the timings come from.

